WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.910
If you're not a developer, it's possible

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:03.830
that you may not have heard of GitHub

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:06.030
before. But GitHub is actually quite an

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:07.990
important website and it's becoming more

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.030
and more important as these agentic

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:11.870
platforms are evolving and it's

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:14.230
practically making everyone a developer

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:16.110
on their own right. So GitHub, which you

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:18.070
can access on github.com, you can think

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:20.990
of it as the world's Google Drive but

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.990
for code and for development. Then it's

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.310
slowly but surely becoming the world's

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:27.630
Google Drive for AI agents. And it's

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:29.510
quite an important website to at least

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:32.150
be familiar with because a lot of the

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:33.950
tools that are coming out in the agentic

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:36.310
platform space are actually hosted on

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:38.710
GitHub. So to give an example, this tool

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:41.630
called VideoUse is a tool for agents

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:44.070
that let you edit videos automatically.

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:45.670
And if you want to use this, all you

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:48.470
need to do really is to copy the URL of

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:50.150
this GitHub link. And if you send it to

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:53.270
Claude Code and ask it to install this

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:55.510
repo, [snorts] stands for repository or

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:57.350
a GitHub repository, which is basically

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:59.590
just a folder that contains some code

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:01.590
that you can think of as like a Google

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:03.550
Drive folder, essentially shared to the

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:05.430
world is what it is. You can see here

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:07.270
that it is starting by checking the

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:09.110
repo's readme, analyzing the whole

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:11.750
thing, and seeing if it's all safe. Now

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:13.390
as part of this course and in your

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:15.150
agentic AI journey, you'll probably

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:17.350
install a few GitHub repositories or

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:19.190
two. And so what I advise you to do is

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.270
to actually get this skill that I have

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:23.230
called personalize because number one,

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:24.830
once you grab this link and send it to

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:26.830
Claude Code, then you'll be able to just

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:29.030
set up GitHub on your space essentially

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:30.870
so that you can grab other tools that

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:32.470
are hosted in this very important

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:35.110
website. The second thing is that this

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:37.750
skill by itself, personalize, if I open

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:39.830
that, which is just this markdown file,

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.350
that actually gives Claude Code some

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:44.310
instructions on how to personalize any

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:47.470
GitHub repo that you wish to install. So

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:49.310
the more that you build up your whole

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:51.150
workspace, your second brain, or your

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:52.990
operating system, then what this skill

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:55.830
does is it just gives Claude Code these

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:57.870
instructions to check all the tools that

00:01:57.880 --> 00:01:59.590
you're installing to make sure that they

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:02.350
are fit for purpose depending on your

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:04.110
own context and the work that you do.

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:05.630
And so, to install this skill, you can

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:07.670
just copy this URL, which I'll also link

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:09.109
down below. And if you give that to

00:02:09.119 --> 00:02:11.390
Cloud Code, say install this skill, what

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.470
will happen firstly is it'll probably

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:16.070
tell you to install the software called

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:18.030
Git if in case you don't have that yet.

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:19.830
Now, the good news is Git is open

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:21.470
source. It's one of the most trusted

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:23.350
pieces of software in the world, and

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:26.030
that is just the essential component for

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:28.270
you to grab files from GitHub. So,

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:30.150
traditionally to install this, you would

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:32.590
need to go to this website, install it,

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:33.990
and actually run through the setup

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:36.110
yourself. But with Cloud Code, you can

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:37.949
just give it permission to grab Git from

00:02:37.959 --> 00:02:40.190
the web and install it on your computer.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:41.870
For me, since I already have Git

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:43.510
installed, you can see that it just went

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:46.190
ahead and installed Personalize for me.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:48.590
And it also gives me a quick overview of

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:50.310
what it is about. So, now let's say we

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:52.470
want to install this tool. If we copy

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:54.510
the URL, send that to Cloud Code, and

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:56.910
just type in /personalize,

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:58.270
you should now have that slash command

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:00.229
that will invoke that skill. And now,

00:03:00.239 --> 00:03:02.550
instead of just blindly installing that

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:04.830
skill, you can just use personalize,

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:06.630
which you can see here it is starting to

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:08.270
use that skill now, which just means

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:10.070
that it reads those instructions that

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:11.830
are contained in that skill. What it

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:14.630
will just do is give a concrete opinion

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:16.750
on whether this is useful to you, how it

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:18.470
will apply, so that no matter what new

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:20.710
tool you add in, especially once you

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:23.110
have sort of solidified your workspace,

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:24.670
then you'll be able to install it with a

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:27.390
bit more wisdom than just blindly

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:29.270
putting it up and adding it to your

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:30.870
growing workspace. And so, for me, you

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:32.870
can see that it provides a description

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:34.630
of what this tool is about, what is the

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:37.190
take rate, meaning how good it is for my

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:39.310
own setup, and also a recommendation on

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:41.150
where it fits versus what I already

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:43.350
have. So, there that is GitHub in a

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:45.509
nutshell, very useful. And GitHub is

00:03:45.519 --> 00:03:47.870
also in a way sort of a social media

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:50.470
website of sorts. So, I advise you to

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:52.630
also sign up to it because in the future

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:55.390
you may be interested to have Cloud Code

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:57.590
put out repositories or basically shared

00:03:57.600 --> 00:03:59.070
code that you want to share with the

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:00.670
world. Like for example, Open Claw,

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:03.310
which is a popular 24/7 agent assistant

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:05.710
that is also hosted and was just shared

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:07.430
by its creator and just made it open

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:09.190
source, which means just putting out all

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:12.070
the files of this project over at this

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:14.110
Google Drive for agents. The other

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:16.470
useful website that is related is this

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:19.270
one called star-history.com

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:21.710
because what star-history.com does is it

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:24.230
just gives a leaderboard on which GitHub

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:26.630
projects are actually trending. And so

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:28.510
if you look here at the left, there are

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:30.510
a lot of GitHub projects here that you

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:32.510
can find and see. And a lot of the times

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:34.190
when I am trying to find like a good

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:36.150
project for my agentic coding platform

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:37.990
and setup or stuff that I think would be

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:40.190
useful for our community, I often find

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:42.230
it here because these are the ones that

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:44.870
are trending in terms of the amount of

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:46.470
GitHub stars that they get. And by

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:48.790
GitHub stars, it is literally this one.

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:50.990
It is sort of like giving a favorite or

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:54.110
a like for your open source repo so that

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:56.750
people can discover it in websites like

00:04:56.760 --> 00:04:58.590
star-history. So they're definitely

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:00.710
advice for you to bookmark this website

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:03.150
and check back often once you get into

00:05:03.160 --> 00:05:07.240
that habit of using Cloud Code.
